/-!
# Bounded solvability of systems over a free group is primitive recursive

A finite system of equations and inequations over the free group `F(A)` is coded by its two lists
of words in the variables and the letters of `A`; the words are arbitrary, possibly unreduced. A
sub-basis constraint is coded by a finite list of pairs `(x, a)`
(`TauCeti.EqIneqSystem.constraintOfList`): the variable `x` may only take values in the subgroup
generated by the letters `a` listed with it, and a variable that does not occur in the list must
take the value `1`. The relation

> the system coded by `p` has a solution in `F(A)` under the constraint coded by `l`, all of
> whose values have length at most `N`

is primitive recursive in `l`, `p` and `N`, for every primitively encodable alphabet of variables
`X` and every primitively encodable alphabet `A`, which need not be finite
(`TauCeti.EqIneqSystem.primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution`); for `X = ℕ` the number
of variables is not fixed. For a finite alphabet `A` the same holds without constraint
(`TauCeti.EqIneqSystem.primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isSolution`), since allowing every letter for
the variables occurring in the system, and none for the others, constrains nothing. Consequently,
a computable bound on the length of a shortest solution makes solvability, with or without
constraint, a computable predicate of the code
(`TauCeti.EqIneqSystem.computablePred_exists_isConstrainedSolution_of_norm_le`,
`TauCeti.EqIneqSystem.computablePred_exists_isSolution_of_norm_le`).

Constrained solvability is the problem to which the positive theory of a nonabelian free group of
finite rank reduces. Let `A` be finite with at least two letters. By Merzljakov's theorem, and
conversely by specializing the letters `xᵢ`, a positive sentence `∀ x₁ ∃ y₁ … ∀ xₖ ∃ yₖ, S = 1`
holds in `F(A)` exactly when the equation `S = 1`, read over the free group on `A` and the letters
`x₁, …, xₖ`, has a solution in which each `yᵢ` lies in the subgroup generated by `A` and
`x₁, …, xᵢ`. These subgroups are coded by a finite list of pairs, and the relation evaluated at a
computable bound on the length of a shortest constrained solution decides this constrained
solvability.

The procedure is the exhaustive search by which a recursive bound on the length of a shortest
solution yields Makanin's decidability theorem: only the variables named by the constraint
matter, the others taking the value `1`
(`TauCeti.EqIneqSystem.IsConstrainedSolution.eq_one_of_forall_notMem`); there are finitely many
tuples of words of length at most `N` in the letters allowed for each of them
(`FreeGroup.wordsOverOfLengthLE`); and each tuple is tested by substitution and free reduction
(`TauCeti.EqIneqSystem.primrecRel_isSolution_mk_getD`). A variable alphabet `X` other than `ℕ` is
renamed into `ℕ` by the codes of its elements.

## References

* G. S. Makanin, *Decidability of the universal and positive theories of a free group*,
  Math. USSR-Izv. 25 (1985), 75–88, §3, proof of Theorem 1.
* O. Kharlampovich, A. Myasnikov, *Implicit function theorem over free groups*, J. Algebra 290
  (2005), §4.4: Merzljakov's theorem, and Corollary 9 with its proof (the positive theory is
  decided by solvability of equations with the constraints `yᵢ ∈ F[Xᵢ]`).
* V. Diekert, A. Jez, W. Plandowski, *Finding all solutions of equations in free groups and
  monoids with involution*, Inform. and Comput. 251 (2016), §1–§2: equations with constraints,
  the alphabet and the set of variables being part of the input.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.EqIneqSystem

open FreeGroup

variable {A : Type*}

/-- A table of words solves a system exactly when its substitution into every equation
reduces to the empty word and its substitution into every inequation does not. -/
private theorem isSolution_mk_getD_iff
    (p : List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)))
    (u : List (List (A × Bool))) :
    (ofWords p).IsSolution (fun x => FreeGroup.mk (u.getD x [])) of ↔
      (∀ w ∈ p.1, FreeGroup.mk (substituteVars (fun x => u.getD x []) w) = 1) ∧
        ∀ w ∈ p.2, ¬ FreeGroup.mk (substituteVars (fun x => u.getD x []) w) = 1 := by
  simp [isSolution_ofWords_iff, mk_substituteVars, eval_eq_lift]

/-- Whether a table of words solves a system is primitive recursive in the table and the
system. The `x`-th word of the table represents the value of the variable `x`, the variables
beyond the table take the value `1`, and the letters of `A` stand for themselves. -/
theorem primrecRel_isSolution_mk_getD [Primcodable A] :
    PrimrecRel fun (u : List (List (A × Bool)))
        (p : List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool))) =>
      (ofWords p).IsSolution (fun x => FreeGroup.mk (u.getD x [])) of := by
  have h : PrimrecRel fun (w : List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) (u : List (List (A × Bool))) =>
      FreeGroup.mk (substituteVars (fun x => u.getD x []) w) = 1 :=
    primrecPred_mk_eq_one.comp (primrec₂_substituteVars_getD.comp Primrec.snd Primrec.fst)
  exact ((h.forall_mem_list.comp (Primrec.fst.comp Primrec.snd) Primrec.fst).and
    (h.not.forall_mem_list.comp (Primrec.snd.comp Primrec.snd) Primrec.fst)).of_eq
      fun q => (isSolution_mk_getD_iff q.2 q.1).symm

section Constrained

/-- The letters listed with the variable `x`. -/
private def allowedLetters (l : List (ℕ × A)) (x : ℕ) : List A :=
  l.filterMap fun y => if y.1 = x then some y.2 else none

private theorem mem_allowedLetters {l : List (ℕ × A)} {x : ℕ} {a : A} :
    a ∈ allowedLetters l x ↔ (x, a) ∈ l := by
  simp [allowedLetters]

/-- A number exceeding every variable listed in a constraint. -/
private def constraintBound (l : List (ℕ × A)) : ℕ :=
  (l.map Prod.fst).sum + 1

private theorem lt_constraintBound {l : List (ℕ × A)} {x : ℕ} {a : A} (h : (x, a) ∈ l) :
    x < constraintBound l :=
  Nat.lt_succ_of_le (List.le_sum_of_mem (List.mem_map_of_mem (f := Prod.fst) h))

/-- The tuples of words tested for a constrained system: for each variable below the bound,
one word of length at most `N` in its allowed letters. -/
private def constrainedCandidates (l : List (ℕ × A)) (N : ℕ) : List (List (List (A × Bool))) :=
  ((List.range (constraintBound l)).map fun x =>
    wordsOverOfLengthLE (allowedLetters l x) N).sections

/-- Every word of a tested tuple has length at most `N` and uses only allowed letters; beyond
the tuple the word is empty. -/
private theorem getD_of_mem_constrainedCandidates {l : List (ℕ × A)} {N : ℕ}
    {u : List (List (A × Bool))} (hu : u ∈ constrainedCandidates l N) (x : ℕ) :
    (u.getD x []).length ≤ N ∧ ∀ y ∈ u.getD x [], (x, y.1) ∈ l := by
  rw [constrainedCandidates, List.mem_sections] at hu
  rcases lt_or_ge x u.length with hx | hx
  · have h := hu.get hx (hu.length_eq ▸ hx)
    simp only [List.get_eq_getElem, List.getElem_map, List.getElem_range,
      mem_wordsOverOfLengthLE, mem_allowedLetters] at h
    rwa [List.getD_eq_getElem _ _ hx]
  · rw [List.getD_eq_default _ _ hx]
    simp

/-- The reduced words of the values below the bound form a tested tuple, when the values have
length at most `N` and use only allowed letters. -/
private theorem map_toWord_mem_constrainedCandidates [DecidableEq A] {l : List (ℕ × A)} {N : ℕ}
    {v : ℕ → FreeGroup A} (hv : ∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N)
    (hl : ∀ x, ∀ y ∈ (v x).toWord, (x, y.1) ∈ l) :
    (List.range (constraintBound l)).map (fun x => (v x).toWord) ∈
      constrainedCandidates l N := by
  rw [constrainedCandidates, List.mem_sections, List.forall₂_map_left_iff,
    List.forall₂_map_right_iff, List.forall₂_same]
  exact fun x _ => mem_wordsOverOfLengthLE.2
    ⟨hv x, fun y hy => mem_allowedLetters.2 (hl x y hy)⟩

/-- A system has a constrained solution with all values of length at most `N` exactly when one
of the finitely many tested tuples of words solves it. -/
private theorem exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution_iff [DecidableEq A] (l : List (ℕ × A))
    (p : List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool))) (N : ℕ) :
    (∃ v : ℕ → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧
        (ofWords p).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList l) v of) ↔
      ∃ u ∈ constrainedCandidates l N,
        (ofWords p).IsSolution (fun x => FreeGroup.mk (u.getD x [])) of := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨v, hv, hs⟩
    refine ⟨_, map_toWord_mem_constrainedCandidates hv fun x y hy =>
      mem_constraintOfList.1 (((isConstrainedSolution_iff_toWord _ _ _).1 hs).2 x y hy), ?_⟩
    convert hs.isSolution using 1
    funext x
    rcases lt_or_ge x (constraintBound l) with hx | hx
    · simp [hx, mk_toWord]
    · rw [List.getD_eq_default _ _ (by simpa using hx), ← one_eq_mk]
      exact (hs.eq_one_of_forall_notMem fun a ha => hx.not_gt (lt_constraintBound ha)).symm
  · rintro ⟨u, hu, hs⟩
    refine ⟨_, fun x => norm_mk_le.trans (getD_of_mem_constrainedCandidates hu x).1,
      hs.isConstrainedSolution fun x => ?_⟩
    simpa only [lift_of_apply] using lift_mk_mem_closure_image of fun y hy =>
      mem_constraintOfList.2 ((getD_of_mem_constrainedCandidates hu x).2 y hy)

/-- Bounded constrained solvability is unchanged when the variables are renamed by their codes:
the numbers that are not codes are named by no listed pair, so they take the value `1`. -/
private theorem exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution_relabel_encode_iff {X : Type*}
    [Encodable X] [DecidableEq A] (l : List (X × A)) (S : EqIneqSystem X A) (N : ℕ) :
    (∃ v : ℕ → FreeGroup A, (∀ n, (v n).norm ≤ N) ∧
        (S.relabel Encodable.encode).IsConstrainedSolution
          (constraintOfList (l.map (Prod.map Encodable.encode id))) v of) ↔
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧
        S.IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList l) v of := by
  have hC := constraintOfList_map_prodMap (Encodable.encode_injective (α := X)) l
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨v, hv, hs⟩
    refine ⟨v ∘ Encodable.encode, fun x => hv _, ?_⟩
    simpa only [Function.comp_def, hC] using hs.of_relabel
  · rintro ⟨v, hv, hs⟩
    refine ⟨fun n => (Encodable.decode₂ X n).elim 1 v, fun n => ?_,
      IsSolution.isConstrainedSolution ?_ fun n => ?_⟩
    · cases h : Encodable.decode₂ X n <;> simp [h, hv]
    · simpa [Function.comp_def, Encodable.encodek₂] using hs.isSolution
    · cases h : Encodable.decode₂ X n with
      | none => exact one_mem _
      | some x =>
        obtain rfl := Encodable.mem_decode₂.1 h
        simpa [Encodable.encodek₂, hC] using hs.mem_closure x

variable [Primcodable A]

private theorem primrec₂_constrainedCandidates : Primrec₂ (constrainedCandidates (A := A)) := by
  have hl : Primrec₂ (allowedLetters (A := A)) :=
    Primrec.listFilterMap Primrec.fst (Primrec.ite
      (Primrec.eq.comp (Primrec.fst.comp Primrec.snd) (Primrec.snd.comp Primrec.fst))
      (Primrec.option_some.comp (Primrec.snd.comp Primrec.snd)) (Primrec.const none)).to₂
  have hb : Primrec (constraintBound (A := A)) :=
    Primrec.succ.comp ((Primrec.list_sum Primrec.nat_add).comp
      (Primrec.list_map Primrec.id (Primrec.fst.comp Primrec.snd).to₂))
  exact (Primrec.list_sections.comp (Primrec.list_map
    (Primrec.list_range.comp (hb.comp Primrec.fst))
    (primrec₂_wordsOverOfLengthLE.comp (hl.comp (Primrec.fst.comp Primrec.fst) Primrec.snd)
      (Primrec.snd.comp Primrec.fst)).to₂)).to₂

private theorem primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution_nat [DecidableEq A] :
    PrimrecRel fun (q : List (ℕ × A) ×
        (List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)))) (N : ℕ) =>
      ∃ v : ℕ → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧
        (ofWords q.2).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList q.1) v of :=
  (primrecRel_isSolution_mk_getD.exists_mem_list.comp
    (primrec₂_constrainedCandidates.comp (Primrec.fst.comp Primrec.fst) Primrec.snd)
    (Primrec.snd.comp Primrec.fst)).of_eq fun q =>
      (exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution_iff q.1.1 q.1.2 q.2).symm

/-- **Bounded solvability under sub-basis constraints is primitive recursive.** For a primitively
encodable alphabet of variables `X`, it is a primitive-recursive relation of a list of allowed
pairs, a pair of lists of words in the variables and the letters of `A`, and a number `N`, whether
the system has a solution in `F(A)` all of whose values have length at most `N` and lie in the
subgroups generated by the allowed letters. The words need not be reduced and the alphabet `A`
need not be finite; for `X = ℕ` the number of variables is not fixed. -/
theorem primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution {X : Type*} [Primcodable X]
    [DecidableEq A] :
    PrimrecRel fun (q : List (X × A) ×
        (List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)))) (N : ℕ) =>
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧
        (ofWords q.2).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList q.1) v of := by
  have hl : Primrec fun l : List (X × A) => l.map (Prod.map Encodable.encode id) :=
    Primrec.list_map .id ((Primrec.prodMap .encode .id).comp .snd).to₂
  have hy : Primrec fun y : (X ⊕ A) × Bool => (Sum.map Encodable.encode id y.1, y.2) :=
    ((Primrec.sumMap .encode .id).comp .fst).pair .snd
  have hr : Primrec fun l : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) =>
      l.map (List.map fun y => (Sum.map Encodable.encode id y.1, y.2)) :=
    Primrec.list_map .id (Primrec.list_map .snd (hy.comp .snd).to₂).to₂
  refine (primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution_nat.comp
    ((hl.comp Primrec.fst).pair ((hr.comp (Primrec.fst.comp Primrec.snd)).pair
      (hr.comp (Primrec.snd.comp Primrec.snd))) |>.comp Primrec.fst) Primrec.snd).of_eq
    fun q => ?_
  rw [← relabel_ofWords]
  exact exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution_relabel_encode_iff q.1.1 (ofWords q.1.2) q.2

/-- **Constrained solvability is decidable given a computable length bound.** If `B` is a
computable function of a list of allowed pairs and the code of a system such that every system
with a constrained solution has one all of whose values have length at most `B`, then
solvability in `F(A)` under the constraint is a computable predicate of the list and the code. -/
theorem computablePred_exists_isConstrainedSolution_of_norm_le {X : Type*} [Primcodable X]
    [DecidableEq A]
    {B : List (X × A) × (List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool))) → ℕ}
    (hB : Computable B)
    (h : ∀ q, (∃ v : X → FreeGroup A,
        (ofWords q.2).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList q.1) v of) →
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ B q) ∧
        (ofWords q.2).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList q.1) v of) :
    ComputablePred fun q : List (X × A) ×
        (List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool))) =>
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (ofWords q.2).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList q.1) v of := by
  obtain ⟨_, hR⟩ := primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution (A := A) (X := X)
  exact (Computable.computablePred (hR.to_comp.comp (Computable.id.pair hB))).of_eq
    fun q => ⟨fun ⟨v, _, hv⟩ => ⟨v, hv⟩, h q⟩

end Constrained

section Unconstrained

variable {X : Type*}

/-- The variables occurring in the words of a system. -/
private def varsOfWords (p : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool))) :
    List X :=
  (p.1 ++ p.2).flatten.filterMap fun y => y.1.getLeft?

private theorem mem_varsOfWords
    {p : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool))}
    {w : List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)} (hw : w ∈ p.1 ++ p.2) {x : X} {b : Bool}
    (hx : (Sum.inl x, b) ∈ w) : x ∈ varsOfWords p :=
  List.mem_filterMap.2 ⟨_, List.mem_flatten_of_mem hw hx, rfl⟩

variable [Finite A]

/-- The constraint allowing every letter for each variable occurring in a system. -/
private noncomputable def fullConstraint
    (p : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool))) : List (X × A) :=
  varsOfWords p ×ˢ (Set.finite_univ (α := A)).toFinset.toList

/-- A system has a solution with all values of length at most `N` exactly when it has one under
the constraint allowing every letter for the variables occurring in it: the other variables may
take the value `1`. -/
private theorem exists_norm_le_isSolution_iff_isConstrainedSolution [DecidableEq A]
    (p : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool))) (N : ℕ) :
    (∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧ (ofWords p).IsSolution v of) ↔
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧
        (ofWords p).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList (fullConstraint p)) v of := by
  classical
  refine ⟨fun ⟨v, hv, hs⟩ => ?_, fun ⟨v, hv, hs⟩ => ⟨v, hv, hs.isSolution⟩⟩
  refine ⟨fun x => if x ∈ varsOfWords p then v x else 1, fun x => ?_,
    ((isSolution_ofWords_congr of fun w hw x b hx => ?_).1 hs).isConstrainedSolution fun x => ?_⟩
  · dsimp only
    split_ifs <;> simp [hv]
  · simp [mem_varsOfWords hw hx]
  · split_ifs with hx
    · have hC : constraintOfList (fullConstraint p) x = Set.univ := by
        ext a
        simp [fullConstraint, hx]
      simp [hC, closure_range_of]
    · exact one_mem _

variable [Primcodable A] [DecidableEq A] [Primcodable X]

/-- **Bounded solvability is primitive recursive.** For a finite alphabet `A` and a primitively
encodable alphabet of variables `X`, it is a primitive-recursive relation of a pair of lists of
words in the variables and the letters of `A`, and of a number `N`, whether the system with these
equations and inequations has a solution in `F(A)` all of whose values have length at most `N`.
The words need not be reduced; for `X = ℕ` the number of variables is not fixed. -/
theorem primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isSolution :
    PrimrecRel fun (p : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool))) (N : ℕ) =>
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧ (ofWords p).IsSolution v of := by
  have hget : Primrec (Sum.getLeft? : X ⊕ A → Option X) :=
    (Primrec.sumCasesOn Primrec.id (Primrec.option_some.comp Primrec.snd).to₂
      (Primrec.const none).to₂).of_eq fun y => by cases y <;> rfl
  have hc : Primrec (fullConstraint (X := X) (A := A)) :=
    Primrec.list_product.comp (Primrec.listFilterMap
      (Primrec.list_flatten.comp (Primrec.list_append.comp Primrec.fst Primrec.snd))
      (hget.comp (Primrec.fst.comp Primrec.snd)).to₂) (Primrec.const _)
  exact (primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isConstrainedSolution.comp
    ((hc.pair Primrec.id).comp Primrec.fst) Primrec.snd).of_eq fun q =>
      (exists_norm_le_isSolution_iff_isConstrainedSolution q.1 q.2).symm

/-- **Solvability is decidable given a computable length bound.** If `B` is a computable
function of the code of a system such that every solvable system `p` has a solution all of
whose values have length at most `B p`, then solvability in `F(A)` is a computable predicate
of the code. -/
theorem computablePred_exists_isSolution_of_norm_le
    {B : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) → ℕ} (hB : Computable B)
    (h : ∀ p, (∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (ofWords p).IsSolution v of) →
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ B p) ∧ (ofWords p).IsSolution v of) :
    ComputablePred fun p : List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((X ⊕ A) × Bool)) =>
      ∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (ofWords p).IsSolution v of := by
  obtain ⟨_, hR⟩ := primrecRel_exists_norm_le_isSolution (A := A) (X := X)
  exact (Computable.computablePred (hR.to_comp.comp (Computable.id.pair hB))).of_eq
    fun p => ⟨fun ⟨v, _, hv⟩ => ⟨v, hv⟩, h p⟩

end Unconstrained

section Examples

variable [DecidableEq A]

/-- The inequation `x ≠ 1` has a solution with values of length at most `N` exactly when
`N` is positive and the alphabet is nonempty: the bound matters, and at rank zero every
inequation fails. -/
theorem exists_norm_le_isSolution_var_ne_one_iff {X : Type*} (x₀ : X) (N : ℕ) :
    (∃ v : X → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ N) ∧
      (ofWords (X := X) (A := A) ([], [[(Sum.inl x₀, true)]])).IsSolution v of) ↔
      0 < N ∧ Nonempty A := by
  have hone : ∀ v : X → FreeGroup A,
      eval v of (FreeGroup.mk [((Sum.inl x₀ : X ⊕ A), true)]) = v x₀ := fun v => eval_of v of _
  simp only [isSolution_ofWords_iff, List.not_mem_nil, false_imp_iff, implies_true, true_and,
    List.mem_singleton, forall_eq, hone]
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨v, hv, h0⟩
    refine ⟨(Nat.pos_of_ne_zero fun h => h0 (norm_eq_zero.mp h)).trans_le (hv x₀), ?_⟩
    by_contra hA
    rw [not_nonempty_iff] at hA
    exact h0 (Subsingleton.elim _ _)
  · rintro ⟨hN, ⟨a⟩⟩
    exact ⟨fun _ => of a, fun _ => by simpa using Nat.succ_le_of_lt hN, of_ne_one a⟩

/-- The empty system is solved by the all-identity assignment, of length zero. -/
example : ∃ v : ℕ → FreeGroup A, (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ 0) ∧
    (ofWords (X := ℕ) (A := A) ([], [])).IsSolution v of :=
  ⟨fun _ => 1, by simp, by simp [isSolution_ofWords_iff]⟩

/-- The equation `[x, y] = [a, b]`, written as the unreduced word `x y x⁻¹ y⁻¹ b a b⁻¹ a⁻¹`,
has the solution `x = a`, `y = b` with values of length one. -/
example : ∃ v : ℕ → FreeGroup (Fin 2), (∀ x, (v x).norm ≤ 1) ∧
    (ofWords (X := ℕ) (A := Fin 2) ([[(Sum.inl 0, true), (Sum.inl 1, true), (Sum.inl 0, false),
      (Sum.inl 1, false), (Sum.inr 1, true), (Sum.inr 0, true), (Sum.inr 1, false),
      (Sum.inr 0, false)]], [])).IsSolution v of := by
  refine ⟨fun x => if x = 0 then of 0 else of 1, fun x => ?_, ?_⟩
  · dsimp only
    split <;> simp
  · simp [isSolution_ofWords_iff, eval_eq_lift, lift_mk]

/-- At rank zero the bound zero works for every system, so solvability over the trivial group
is a computable predicate of the code. -/
example [IsEmpty A] [Primcodable A] :
    ComputablePred fun p : List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) =>
      ∃ v : ℕ → FreeGroup A, (ofWords p).IsSolution v of :=
  computablePred_exists_isSolution_of_norm_le (B := fun _ => 0) (Computable.const 0)
    fun _ ⟨v, hv⟩ => ⟨v, fun _ => (norm_eq_zero.mpr (Subsingleton.elim _ _)).le, hv⟩

/-- At rank zero the bound zero works for every system under every constraint, so constrained
solvability over the trivial group is a computable predicate of the list and the code. -/
example [IsEmpty A] [Primcodable A] :
    ComputablePred fun q : List (ℕ × A) ×
        (List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool)) × List (List ((ℕ ⊕ A) × Bool))) =>
      ∃ v : ℕ → FreeGroup A, (ofWords q.2).IsConstrainedSolution (constraintOfList q.1) v of :=
  computablePred_exists_isConstrainedSolution_of_norm_le (B := fun _ => 0) (Computable.const 0)
    fun _ ⟨v, hv⟩ => ⟨v, fun _ => (norm_eq_zero.mpr (Subsingleton.elim _ _)).le, hv⟩

end Examples

end TauCeti.EqIneqSystem
